    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Type foundry founded 2007 by Paul Barnes and Christian Schwartz, based in New York and London (own About page, corroborated by Wikipedia and Communication Arts). Best known for the Guardian Egyptian redesign (D&AD Black Pencil) and widely used retail faces such as Graphik, Publico, Canela and Caslon Doric; also runs a Design Studio arm doing custom identity and logotype work for editorial, cultural and retail clients. About page names 11 in-house partners and staff (Barnes, Schwartz plus 9 named type designers, studio manager, licensing and design-studio directors), so sized 11-40 rather than the migration default of 2-10; separately lists ~20 published typeface designers and ~19 outside collaborators who are contributors, not employees.",
